-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  driver_dev_pack.adam - adam --dev-pack <spec> (PLAN-LINUX64 PK4) on the
  command line: the argument after the hidden switch is its spec, never a
  command (DoCommandAt skips it); a spec that is not there is read as one,
  PACK FAILED names it relative to its folder, exit code 1. The archives a
  good spec writes are exe.exe_dev_pack's (Adam.Dev.Pack in-process).
*******************************************************************************/

/*
@@test
  kind cli
  args "--no-banner" "--dev-pack" "<DIR>/driver_dev_pack_none.toml"
  exitcode 1
  | Pack spec <DIR>/driver_dev_pack_none.toml
  | PACK FAILED - driver_dev_pack_none.toml: the file cannot be read
@@end
*/

module exe driver_dev_pack;

begin
end.
